BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open Mic at the Custom House Maritime Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261228
DTSTAMP:20261017T140337Z
UID:0d87efb1ef8bf41cf100a558adc3@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Come for the creativity\, stay for the camaraderie. Our monthl
 y Open Mic is all about good vibes and real connection. Hosted by Kenny 'D
 oc' Frasier\, it’s a welcoming space for music\, poetry\, prose\, stand-
 up—or just saying what’s on your mind. This is a laid-back\, live show
  where anyone can show up and share a few minutes on the mic. Try out new 
 material\, build your confidence\, or just soak in the energy—it’s all
  fair game. And there are cookies! All ages\, all abilities are welcome.\n
 \nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/open-mic-custom-house-maritime-museum
LOCATION:Custom House Maritime Museum\, Custom House Maritime Museum\, 150
  Bank Street\, New London CT\, 06320
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/open-mic-custom-house-maritime-museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fashioning America: 250 Years of Greenwich Style
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260805
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270111
DTSTAMP:20261017T140337Z
UID:0bf32255b521fb9c49ace966b884@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Greenwich Historical Society presents the third and final exhi
 bition in the series celebrating America’s 250th—Fashioning America: 2
 50 years of Greenwich Style\, chronicling the evolution of American fashio
 n and how these styles reflect changes in American society and culture. Fo
 r 250 years\, the ideals of the American Revolution\, as expressed in the 
 Declaration of Independence\, have helped shape our national identity—an
 d these enduring principles are reflected in the fashions we have worn thr
 oughout history and choose to wear today.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/e
 vents/fashioning-america-250-years-greenwich-style
LOCATION:Greenwich Historical Society\, 47 Strickland road\, Cos Cob CT\, 
 06807
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/fashioning-america-250-years-greenwich-styl
 e
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Snow Goose
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTSTAMP:20261017T140337Z
UID:d7dfb517017918bc91154e4caf72@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:On the windswept coast of England an unlikely bond forms betwe
 en Philip\, a reclusive artist shunned by society\, and Frith\, a resilien
 t young woman\, when they rescue a wounded snow goose. With World War II l
 ooming\, their friendship allows her to imagine a life beyond her village
 \, and him to confront his own humanity as he sets sail on a daring journe
 y to save soldiers trapped at Dunkirk. Discover an unforgettable new music
 al with a soaring score that will fill your heart.\n\nSource: https://ctvi
 sit.com/events/snow-goose
LOCATION:The Goodspeed\, 6 Main Street\, East Haddam CT\, 06423
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/snow-goose
END:VEVENT
